The support desk handles all products, not only `sched-prod`. Keep one ticket per supported
cause, preserving each unique report ID and its received/merged times. Subject matching finds
candidates; it does not establish duplicates. This replaces the stale subject-only guidance
under [decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause/).

## Current rule

1. Read the report's body, affected product, behavior, input/output and relevant configuration.
2. Compare evidence of the mechanism with candidate tickets. For date reports, resolve the
   tenant locale, booking form and channel; intake browser locale and tags are only guesses.
3. Merge only when the evidence supports the same cause, even if the subjects differ.
4. Keep different causes apart even when their subjects match. If the tenant, mechanism or
   evidence is missing, put the report in investigation and request the missing details.
5. Count unique IDs once. Preserve contradictory evidence, recalculate after new exports,
   and assign an owner. A “known” label does not prove a fix.

## Date-report examples

<DedupeExplorer />

The examples run the date-specific classifier; use product-specific evidence for other
products. A matching subject with an unknown tenant is not enough to merge.

## Review and history

The [#4471 reassessment](/kb/incidents/4471-reassessment/) shows why the old rule failed.
Accepted [decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject/) is retained unchanged as history;
its June 2024 review date does not make it current. Follow decision 0002 for incoming reports
while the desk tracks separate causes and their outcomes. Review this guidance at the
shared layout's configured interval and when evidence changes.

